# Tulzo Project - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Tulzo is a workflow automation platform built with Next.js 14 (App Router), Supabase, Clerk auth, and MCP (Model Context Protocol).

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 with App Router
- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL + Realtime)
- **Auth**: Clerk (plan checking: `has({ plan: 'pro' })`, `has({ plan: 'plus' })`)
- **UI**: Adobe React Spectrum components
- **AI**: Vercel AI SDK, multiple model providers

## Key Directories
- `app/` - Next.js App Router pages and API routes
- `src/views/` - Large page components (AutomationPage, ChatPage, DashboardPage)
- `src/lib/automation/` - Workflow execution engine
- `src/config/ai-tokens.config.ts` - AI models & pricing (single source of truth)
- `src/types/supabase.ts` - Database types

## Path Aliases
```typescript
// "@/*" → "./*"
import { AI_MODELS } from '@/src/config/ai-tokens.config';
```

## Workflow YAML Schema
Workflows are defined in YAML with these step types:
- `tool:` - MCP tool call (e.g., `brave-search.web_search`)
- `llm:` - AI model call with prompt
- `code:` - JavaScript expression
- `if:` / `for:` / `while:` - Control flow
- `human:` - Human-in-the-loop approval
- `notify:` - Push/email/slack notifications
- `delay:` - Wait N seconds
- `trigger_automation:` - Chain automations
- `wait_for:` - Wait for external variable

## Database Patterns
```typescript
// Always use service role for server-side
const supabase = createClient(
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
  process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY!
);

// Filter by user_id (RLS bypass)
const { data } = await supabase
  .from('automations')
  .select('*')
  .eq('user_id', userId);
```

## API Route Patterns
```typescript
// Export named handlers
export async function GET(req: NextRequest) { ... }
export async function POST(req: NextRequest) { ... }

// Return JSON with error handling
if (!user) {
  return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });
}
```

## OAuth Support
All tool types (MCP, REST, GraphQL, A2A, RAG) support OAuth across:
- Automation execution
- Internal chat
- External surfaces (ChatGPT, Claude Desktop)

Key files:
- `app/api/mcp/route.ts` - Returns `loginUrl` on OAuth error
- `app/api/mcp/oauth-source/route.ts` - Finds OAuth config for tools
- `app/mcp/[serverName]/login/page.tsx` - External OAuth login page

## Coding Standards
- Use TypeScript with explicit types (avoid `any`)
- Use async/await (not .then())
- Destructure props in React components
- Use Supabase RLS with user_id filtering

## Testing
Run workflow tests locally:
```bash
npm run automation <yaml-file>  # Needs TEST_USER_ID in .env.local
```

## Important Files
- `CLAUDE.md` - Full project documentation
- `rules/augment-guidelines.txt` - YAML workflow schema reference
- `src/lib/automation/types.ts` - Workflow type definitions
- `src/lib/automation/executor.ts` - Core workflow executor

